# SNR ladder: does with-K differ from no-K, and stay unbiased, as K/C grows?
# H1+L1, 2-D (mass_ratio, tc), nessai nlive=250, n_pool=8.
#
# SELF-injection (inject the surrogate's own prediction, mismatch=0) so any
# with-K vs no-K difference is PURELY the K-marginalisation, not template
# systematics. Distance sets the SNR: K/C grows ~ SNR^2, so the rungs span from
# C-dominated (SNR~20, with-K == no-K expected) to K-appreciable (SNR~250).
# Same seed => same noise realisation across rungs and across with-K/no-K, so
# the comparison is controlled (single-realisation caveat as always).
#
# netladder_* (DemodGPSurrogate) already ran 2026-07-28 -- see
# results/net_netladder_snr{20,75,250}_{no,with}K*. Confirmed: with-K~=no-K at
# every rung, no bias to SNR~250 -- closes "coverage at SNR>>20" for demod, but
# demod's K is negligible by design so this can't show the log-det bias
# actually appearing.
#
# exactxasladder_* (production exact_xas_lsminq006 checkpoint, K 3-8 orders
# larger, the representation the k_smoothing/q_warping/noise-floor fix stack
# was built against) is the new, currently-queued rung: same distances/
# self-injection/SNR targets, UNSMOOTHED (no --k-smoothing-grid-spacing) so
# the raw bias mechanism is directly comparable against demod's clean result
# at matched SNRs.
universe        = vanilla
executable      = condor/run_net_injection.sh
requirements    = (Machine == "wiay.astro.gla.ac.uk")
request_cpus    = 10
request_memory  = 18432
should_transfer_files = NO
getenv          = false
arguments       = $(tag) 8
output          = condor_logs/net_$(tag).out
error           = condor_logs/net_$(tag).err
log             = condor_logs/net_$(tag).log

queue tag from (
    exactxasladder_snr20_withK
    exactxasladder_snr20_noK
    exactxasladder_snr75_withK
    exactxasladder_snr75_noK
    exactxasladder_snr250_withK
    exactxasladder_snr250_noK
)
